.TH ENV 1 "2026-05-22" "hako" "hako utilities"
.SH NAME
env \- print environment variables
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B env
.RI [ name ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
With no arguments,
.B env
prints every environment variable in
.I KEY=value
format, sorted alphabetically by key, one per line.
.PP
With one or more
.I name
arguments,
.B env
prints only the value of each named variable, one per line.
If any named variable is not set, its name is reported to standard error and
the command exits with status 1 after processing all arguments.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B env
Print all environment variables, sorted.
.TP
.B "env HOME PATH"
Print the values of
.B HOME
and
.B PATH
only.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
One or more requested variables were not set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR env (1),
.BR printenv (1),
.BR hako (1)
